<article class="env-lemma" id="048T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/048T">Lemma <span data-tag="048T">83.5.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme, and let $B$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $j : R \to U \times _ B U$ be a pre-relation over $B$. Then $j_\infty : R_\infty \to U \times _ B U$ is a pre-equivalence relation over $B$. Moreover </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\phi : U \to X$ is $R$-invariant if and only if it is $R_\infty $-invariant, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the canonical map of quotient sheaves $U/R \to U/R_\infty $ (see Groupoids in Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/044H" data-tag="044H">78.19</a>) is an isomorphism, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
weak $R$-orbits agree with weak $R_\infty $-orbits, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R$-orbits agree with $R_\infty $-orbits, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $s, t$ are locally of finite type, then $s_\infty $, $t_\infty $ are locally of finite type, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
add more here as needed. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
